THE FALSE-ABLE CONTROLS. Each is a case ONE question alone PASSES, so a census that asks
either question alone is caught by at least one of them. They drive `classify_one`, the
same function the census classifies with -- not a second implementation of the rule.
  ok   declared+no reader fires (passes (a), fails (b))         want=ORPHAN          got=ORPHAN
  ok   reader+no declaration fires (passes (b), fails (a))      want=UNDECLARED-OPEN got=UNDECLARED-OPEN
  ok   nested under declared parent, neither, fires             want=INERT           got=INERT
  ok   only unbounded reader is UNVERIFIABLE, not opened        want=UNVERIFIABLE    got=UNVERIFIABLE
  ok   the same row with a bounded reader is WITNESSED          want=WITNESSED       got=WITNESSED
  ok   unbounded reader never lands in the ORPHAN cell          want=False           got=False

  6 of 6 controls fire.
  A control that does not fire is a FAIL and this exits 1: a census that fires only on
  the easy case is the `zerogate`/`plantthe46` vacuous-plant class arriving by a THIRD
  door -- a census that AGREES with the property it cannot see.
